# NO-TRACKING environment for the bashy zot verified build.
# Shell-sourceable; shipped as a release asset so a launcher applies exactly
# what this build was gated against. Every knob is documented in
# builds/zot/README.md with its upstream source at the pinned tag.
#
# Usage: set -a; . bashy-build/no-tracking.env; set +a
#
# zot has NO update checker and NO usage reporting. Its entire outbound
# surface is the optional EXTENSIONS, and they are configuration, not
# environment: the shipped bashy-build/config.json keeps "extensions" an
# EMPTY map, which leaves sync (pulls from remote registries), the CVE/trivy
# database download, events and remote metrics all off.
# Upstream reference: project-zot/zot examples/README.md.
#
# The bashy build additionally omits the `ui` build tag, so no web bundle
# fetched from a second upstream repository is linked in at all (see
# builds/zot/README.md §Extension set).
#
# Go's net/http honours the proxy environment, so an operator shell that
# exports a proxy would hand the service an egress path it never asked for.
# Clearing all three and allowing only loopback in NO_PROXY closes that door.
HTTP_PROXY=
HTTPS_PROXY=
http_proxy=
https_proxy=
ALL_PROXY=
all_proxy=
NO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,::1,localhost
no_proxy=127.0.0.1,::1,localhost
